-- What each composed layer filed, per quantity, and the elimination to subtract from it.
# The filed side of a composed layer's sum, beside the elimination it subtracts. One row per layer
# and quantity it states, where that quantity's sum is not suspended, carrying the filed figure and
# the elimination to remove. A layer built from no parts has nothing to subtract and no sum to
# compare.
#
# Fusions that owe no equality are left out
#   A composer who states they never looked for double counting has not claimed their figure equals
#   the sum of its parts, and asserting it anyway is the defect `StatedEliminations` exists to
#   prevent, arriving in the check instead of in the document. `none` and `notApplicable` still owe
#   the sum exactly. Only `unmeasured` suspends it.
#
# It suspends at both levels
#   A fusion may file an elimination and declare its quantity `unmeasured`, "these hours are double
#   counted and nobody can say by how much", which is a different filing from an unsearched list
#   and owes no equality either. `coalesce(e.low, 0)` would read that as a zero and assert a sum
#   the composer declined, and `tests/composition.rs::expected` returns `None` for exactly that
#   case. Two witnesses, one rule, and one relation, composition/suspended_quantities.sqlc, which
#   this anti-joins.
#
# Check the exclusion rather than trusting the count
#   `s.composition IS NULL` is safe only because `composition` is NOT NULL on every arm of
#   suspension_grounds, which composition/suspended_quantities.sqlc carries; a nullable column would
#   keep matched rows silently. The law is worked out again, not recorded, in
#   algebra/composed_quantities.sqlc, every run.
-- layers/summed_quantities.sqlc minus composition/suspended_quantities.sqlc,
-- with eliminations/filed.sqlc.
SELECT d.filing                     AS "filing!",
       d.layer                      AS "layer!",
       d.quantity::text             AS "quantity!",
       d.low::float8                AS "x_low!",
       d.mode::float8               AS "x_mode!",
       d.high::float8               AS "x_high!",
       coalesce(e.low, 0)::float8   AS "e_low!",
       coalesce(e.mode, 0)::float8  AS "e_mode!",
       coalesce(e.high, 0)::float8  AS "e_high!"
FROM      (
    :compose(layers/summed_quantities.sqlc)
) d
LEFT JOIN (
    :compose(composition/suspended_quantities.sqlc)
) s
       ON s.composition = d.filing AND s.composed_layer = d.layer
      AND s.quantity = d.quantity
LEFT JOIN (
    :compose(eliminations/filed.sqlc)
) e
       ON e.composition = d.filing AND e.composed_layer = d.layer
      AND e.quantity = d.quantity
WHERE s.composition IS NULL
  AND d.low IS NOT NULL
